INT. BOWLING ALLEY - PARTY ROOM - DAY

Streamers, a sheet cake, paper plates. Lane 9 thunders next door. A banner reads HAPPY 80TH, GUS.

YOLANDA PRICE (50s) cuts the cake into squares too small for anyone. GUS PRICE (80, her father, party hat crooked) watches the knife.

KENJI PRICE (20s, her son) sits at the end of the table scrolling through his phone. DOROTHEA PRICE (50s, Yolanda's sister, fresh off a flight) drops her coat across a chair and stays standing.

DOROTHEA
Nobody told me it was today.

YOLANDA
I texted you.

DOROTHEA
You texted me Tuesday.

Yolanda sets a plate in front of Gus. Dorothea moves it six inches to the left. Yolanda moves it back. They both let go at the same time.

GUS
I like the corner piece.

Kenji looks up. Yolanda and Dorothea lunge for the cake knife at once. They stop, hands on the handle, faces close.

YOLANDA
I'll do it.

DOROTHEA
You've done everything. Clearly.

She yanks the knife. Frosting smears across the tablecloth. Kenji stands. Gus lifts his hat off his head and sets it on the table, very gently, like a man laying down a hand of cards.

Through the wall, Lane 9 roars. Nobody at the table flinches.
